WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.080
Did you ever wonder if certain foods
have a direct effect on your health?

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.040
Well, I’m here to
solve that mystery

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.480
since you are
the foods you eat.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.560
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.480
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.640
Back by popular demand,
it’s our NutritionFacts Grab Bag,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.400
where we look at the science
on a whole variety of topics

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.240
starting with a story about how to
preserve your sense of smell.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.280
Based on a study
of nearly 2,000 people,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.240
our sense of smell
declines as we age,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.760
similar to our loss in vision
and hearing.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.280
About a quarter of Americans
over the age of 50

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.240
suffer from
olfactory dysfunction,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.440
a difficulty identifying odors,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.360
which climbs to more than half
of individuals

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.560
between the ages
of 65 to 80,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.000
and about 80 percent
in those over the age of 80.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.960
And that was before COVID-19,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:53.800
which affected the smell

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.320
of nearly 50 percent
of sufferers.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.400
Typically, it was temporary,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.800
but as many as a 15 percent

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.800
of non-hospitalized
COVID survivors

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.280
were still experiencing problems
with the ability to smell

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.800
three or more months later,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.040
and there are cases of it
lasting for years.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.720
As anyone with even
a simple head cold can tell you,

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.160
when you lose
your sense of smell,

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.760
you lose much of your sense
of taste as well.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:19.160
Between 75 to 95 percent
of what we think of as taste,

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.400
may actually be smell.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.960
This was all
too vividly illustrated

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.560
by the case
of Algerian War soldiers

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.400
whose tongues
were cut out,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.360
remarkably reporting
little loss

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.960
of food and drink
flavor sensation.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.720
But hey, if loss of smell
leads to loss of taste,

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.960
think of all the weight loss!

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.600
That was apparently the thought

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.920
behind the development
of a "novel nasal device,"

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.000
gag-inducing silicone tubes
you stick into your nostrils

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.920
to cordon off
your smell receptors.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.280
Researchers recorded
a drop in preference

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.480
for sugary foods and beverages
along with weight loss,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.840
but only among
the younger adults,

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.320
presumably because the sense
of smell of the older adults

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.640
was already impaired.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.280
Making everything taste bland

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.240
may help you skip
a few doughnuts,

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.280
but the flipside
is that people

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.200
with smelling difficulties
tend to add more salt.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.080
Older individuals
were found to require

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.000
two to three times more salt
than those who were younger

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.280
to achieve the same salty taste.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.160
It's no wonder
that the lifetime risk

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.840
of developing
high blood pressure

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:30.040
may exceed 90 percent.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.080
What can we do to preserve
our sense of smell?

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.840
Ambient air pollution

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.880
is associated with
olfactory dysfunction,

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.880
thought to explain
why nasal biopsies

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.280
from residents of Mexico City,
living and dead,

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.240
showed more lesions
and inflammatory changes

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.880
than those living
in low-pollution cities.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.000
We may not have a choice
where we live,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.080
but there is definitely
a direct source of air pollution

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.480
tied to loss of smell
we can all choose to avoid:

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.240
cigarette smoke.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.400
Smell loss can have
serious consequences,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.200
for example,

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.920
missing a gas leak, smoke,
or spoiled food.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:11.160
If you have lost your sense
of smell and use natural gas,

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.120
please consider buying
a gas detector.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.080
But, in terms of
direct disability,

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.360
most people who are affected

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.360
don't even to seem to be aware
their smell is impaired,

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.880
even when asked directly.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.080
Nearly 8 out of 10 elderly
individuals with smell loss

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.800
thought they had
normal smell sensitivity.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.080
Hearing loss, however,

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.880
is considered a major cause
of global disability,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.160
ranking among
the top chronic conditions

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.960
affecting older adults.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.400
For far too long, though,

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.840
as a National Academy
of Medicine report put it,

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:42.800
hearing loss has been

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.960
"relegated to the sidelines
of health care."

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:47.760
In our next story,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.680
we look at how duct
tape beat out freezing

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.720
and ten other treatments
for the removal of warts.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.280
When I was reviewing the science behind
common over-the-counter remedies

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:03.240
used in dermatology such as tea
tree oil for acne or nail fungus,

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:08.280
I was surprised to see on the same
page a section on duct tape.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.760
Duct tape?!

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.880
The only time I remember seeing
duct tape used in a medical study

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.960
was on the identification of the gases
responsible for the odor of human farts,

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.880
which involved a collection system
comprised of gas-tight pantaloons

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.640
sealed to the skin with duct tape.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.720
That's the study where they
assessed the wind breaking ability

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.720
of a cushion called
the Toot Trapper.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:36.040
But what the dermatology journal
was talking about is warts.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:39.560
Duct tape brings out our
inventive, slightly kooky side.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.800
Given this versatility, it wasn't
so surprising a few years ago

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:48.360
when a group of doctors reported
that duct tape could get rid of warts.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.760
As I noted in my last wart video,
all sorts of strange things

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.800
are purported to cure warts
because most go away on their own.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.320
A thousand kids were
followed for two years

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.880
and two-thirds of the warts
disappeared without doing a thing.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.840
So maybe we should
just leave them alone,

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.600
although there are cases
that may warrant treatment.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.080
Otherwise we can just let our
own body take care of them.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.120
Warts are caused by wart viruses, and
so spontaneous wart disappearance

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.120
is assumed to be an immune response
where our body finally wakes up

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.600
and takes notice.
This assumption

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.040
is based on studies like this—where
foreign proteins were injected into

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:27.640
the wart itself, like a measles-mumps-
rubella vaccine straight into the wart—

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:32.360
which compared to placebo, appeared to
accelerate the immune clearance process.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:36.640
The problem, of course, is that
injections hurt, and 30% of the kids

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.200
that got their warts injected with the
vaccine suffered a flu-like syndrome.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:44.040
Yikes! OK, scratch that.
What else do we got?

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:48.840
Within a few months any placebo treatment
will work in about a quarter of the cases.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:53.400
So if you put duct tape on 100 warts and
23 go away, that wouldn't mean much.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.640
The traditional medical therapies, acid
treatments and freezing treatments,

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:00.560
bump the cure rate up to about 50%.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.440
So if you were really serious about
testing the efficacy of duct tape,

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.320
you would pit it head to head
against one of those,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.960
and that's exactly what happened.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:15.200
The efficacy of duct tape vs cryotherapy
in the treatment of the common wart.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.480
Cryotherapy is one of the treatments
of choice for many pediatricians.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.960
Objective: To determine if application
of duct tape is as effective

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.040
as cryotherapy in the treatment
of common warts.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.240
Patients were randomized to receive
either liquid nitrogen applied

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.360
to each wart or
duct tape occlusion.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.280
When I heard about treating
warts with duct tape,

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:37.640
I had this image where they were like
trying to rip them off or something.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:42.600
No, no, no, no. They're just applying a
little circle of duct tape every week or so.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:46.040
Although there had been a few
anecdotal reports of using tape,

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:50.760
no prospective, randomized controlled
trial had yet been performed until

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:56.880
this study, which found that the duct
tape was not only equal to but exceeded

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.360
the efficacy of cryotherapy, which
worked in 60% of the cases,

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:04.840
but 85% of the duct tape
patients were cured—significantly

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:08.280
more effective than cryotherapy
for treatment of the common wart.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:12.520
More effective and fewer side effects.
The only adverse effect observed

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.120
in the duct tape group during
our study was a small,

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:21.600
minimal amount of local irritation and
redness, whereas cryotherapy hurts.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.120
You want to hear the saddest thing?

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:29.000
One young child actually vomited in fear
of pain before each cryotherapy session.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.200
They were like torturing the poor kid.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.800
Cryotherapy can cause pain and
bloody blisters that can get infected

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.120
and mess up your nail bed.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:44.640
So, duct tape: more effective, fewer
side effects and more convenient.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.720
Compare applying a little duct tape at
home to making multiple clinic visits,

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.900
dragging the poor kid
back every two weeks.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.280
I mean it's like a win-win-win.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.200
Duct tape can now be offered
as a nonthreatening, painless,

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.880
and inexpensive technique for
the treatment of warts in children.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:03.520
I mean how much does a
little piece of duct tape cost?

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.120
It's like a win-win-win-win.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:11.240
Ah, but the money you save
is the money the doctor loses.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:15.640
There's no way the medical profession is
going to just let this go unchallenged.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:20.520
Further studies were performed
and failed to show an effect,

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.280
and so we end up in the medical
literature with conclusions like this:

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.480
"Is duct tape effective
for treating warts?"

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.440
Bottom line?
No. Huh.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.400
Is duct tape really not
effective after all,

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:39.320
or was there some kind of critical
design flaw in the follow-up studies?

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:43.360
And so even if the effectiveness of duct
tape is shown to be merely equivalent

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:46.640
to that of cryotherapy, it would
be better; and it was shown to be

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.080
even more effective,
in fact maybe most effective.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.920
Compared to 10 other wart treatments,
duct tape beat out them all

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.840
in terms of effectiveness,
and also in terms of cost—

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:01.880
cheaper than all but the DN option,
which stands for Do Nothing.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:04.960
Compared to the most cost-effective
prescription treatments available,

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.840
OTC duct tape, meaning over-the-counter
duct tape, is 10 times cheaper.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:14.080
It's an unusual and welcome event in
health care when a common ailment

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:17.200
is proven equally amenable
to an inexpensive, tolerable,

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.120
and safe alternative therapy.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:20.880
Finally today,

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:26.520
I ask and answer if there really is
such a thing as adrenal fatigue.

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:29.400
Many seeking treatment
for common nonspecific symptoms

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.680
are led to believe
they are suffering

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:34.000
from some sort
of hormonal deficiency.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.200
"Adrenal fatigue"
is the prototypical example.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.360
Chiropractor-coined in 1998,

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.880
the invented diagnosis
has since been embraced

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.520
by naturopaths,
functional medicine,

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.360
and anti-aging doctors.

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.720
But does adrenal fatigue
even exist?

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:55.600
The alleged condition is said
to result from chronic stress

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.400
leading to an "overuse"
of the adrenal glands

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.880
and their eventual
functional decline.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.480
Symptoms supposedly include
fatigue, body aches,

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.800
sleep issues,
and digestive problems,

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.440
at least
according to the websites

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.960
not so coincidentally selling
a suite of supplements

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.400
to remedy it.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.280
It will come as no surprise

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.080
that the originator
of the term

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.680
sells supplements
on his website

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.520
to treat it
for $200 a month.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:23.600
But it may not be
an actual medical condition.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.400
The symptoms people have
are real,

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.720
but they just may be caused
by something else,

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:31.000
for example, sleep apnea,
chronic fatigue syndrome,

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.760
or fibromyalgia.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:36.800
Saliva tests for adrenal
hormone levels are not reliable,

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.240
with studies showing so-called
"adrenal fatigue" patients

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.880
having higher levels
than controls,

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.760
similar levels,
or lower levels,

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:46.760
"an almost systematic finding
of conflicting results."

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:49.880
There is an actual disease
of adrenal insufficiency

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.960
known as Addison's disease,

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.480
which is diagnosed
with an ACTH stimulation test.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:58.760
You inject people with
adrenocorticotropic hormone,

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.560
the signal your brain uses
to get your adrenal glands

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:04.240
to pump out
the stress hormone cortisol,

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:05.960
and if your adrenals
don't respond,

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:08.960
that shows your adrenal glands
must be in trouble.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.000
But inject those
presumed to be suffering

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.080
from chronic stress and fatigue
with ACTH

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:17.320
and sometimes you even get
a greater rise in cortisol,

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:18.760
disproving the notion

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:22.080
that stress causes
the adrenals to "burn out."

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:25.280
But wait,
you were diagnosed with "AF,"

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.880
given corticosteroids,
and now you feel great,

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:30.480
so it must have been real.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.880
That's the thing
about corticosteroids, though.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.520
One of the side effects is
a euphoric sense of well-being.

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:38.480
The problem is
that even low doses

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.920
can increase the risk
of osteoporosis,

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.920
psychiatric and metabolic
disorders, muscle damage,

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:48.680
glaucoma, sleep disturbances,
and cardiovascular diseases.

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:52.360
But wait, you took some
"adrenal support" supplements,

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:53.600
checked the labels,

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.560
confirmed they don't have
any hormones,

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.920
and still felt better.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.240
They lie.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.000
Researchers checked the 12 most
popular adrenal support supplements,

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.080
and every single one
contained hidden hormones,

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.760
none of which were declared
on the product labels.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.480
All contained thyroid hormone

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.640
and most a steroid hormone
as well,

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:19.320
pregnenolone, budesonide,
androstenedione, progesterone,

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.680
cortisone, or cortisol.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:24.880
Adrenal fatigue reminds me
of what used to be called

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.000
"electromagnetic
hypersensitivity,"

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.560
now referred to
in the medical literature

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.200
as "idiopathic
environmental intolerance

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:34.640
attributed to
electromagnetic fields,"

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:37.200
unspecific symptoms
supposedly triggered

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.040
by things like cell phones.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.200
There have been
at least 46 studies

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.400
involving more than 1,000 people
that claim to be affected,

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.320
yet when put to the test
in blinded trials

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.760
the studies
near universally failed

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.360
to show that anyone
could even detect the fields.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.920
Why don't journalists covering
these stories mention the data?

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.200
Because there are
snake-oil salesmen

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:00.560
profiting off
the perceived condition,

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:03.160
selling all matter of
so-called "protective" gadgets

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.080
that viciously attack anyone

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:07.440
even daring to mention
the science,

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.680
accusing them
of denying the reality

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.440
of people's symptoms.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.840
But it's arguably the opposite.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:16.160
They are the ones
hindering sufferers

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.280
from getting to the bottom
of what is actually causing

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:19.360
their symptoms.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.920
Similarly, hawking
unproven tests and treatments

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.840
for adrenal fatigue
could delay the diagnosis

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:28.624
of a real, treatable condition.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.040
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:34.480
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:37.160
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.360
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:45.280
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:48.800
please go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.040
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:55.160
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:57.720
My latest book, “How Not to Age”
is out now,

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:01.440
which premiered at #2 on the
New York Times Best Sellers list.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.720
Check it out at your
local public library.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.080
Of course, all the proceeds
I receive of the sales

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.880
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:14.520
NutritionFacts.org is itself a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:16.360
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:20.400
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.680
Everything on the
website is free.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:23.680
There’s no ads,

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:25.400
no corporate sponsorships,
no kickbacks.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:28.600
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:31.720
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.080
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:39.489
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

